From 19e15b7d6f340dd636e54eb5b39a2991453d8ad5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Teguh Sobirin <teguh@sobir.in>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 17:03:08 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 37/71] ASoC: qcom: common: set jack for codecs on Quaternary
 MI2S

qcom_snd_wcd_jack_setup() only calls snd_soc_component_set_jack() for
the LPI_MI2S_RX_0 and TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_{0,1,2,3} backends. On boards
where a jack-capable codec is wired to the Quaternary MI2S port - such
as the ES8326 headset codec on the Retroid Pocket Duo (eliza) - the
"Headset Jack" is created but never handed to the codec. As a result
the codec's .set_jack op is never invoked, its jack-detection IRQ has
no snd_soc_jack to report to, and headphone insertion/removal and
button events are never delivered to userspace.

Add QUATERNARY_MI2S_RX and QUATERNARY_MI2S_TX to the switch so the
jack is registered with codecs on those DAIs as well.

Signed-off-by: Teguh Sobirin <teguh@sobir.in>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/common.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/common.c b/sound/soc/qcom/common.c
index d9f256d51..c445a5fd0 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/common.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/common.c
@@ -370,6 +370,8 @@ int qcom_snd_wcd_jack_setup(struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd,
 	}
 
 	switch (cpu_dai->id) {
+	case QUATERNARY_MI2S_RX:
+	case QUATERNARY_MI2S_TX:
 	case LPI_MI2S_RX_0:
 	case TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_0:
 	case TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_1:
